tags: stop-notice, stop_grace

A promise of the node: the seconds between the notice and a stop or a hibernation that
the instance did not ask for.

The value is seconds, in base 10. Example: 15. The node sends the notice of the setting
notice (0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:f7bb973c68c1d1101fb628905ad68ed46453bf1c94c374628655cba7391bd3a3) at least this many seconds before it
stops or hibernates the instance. It applies only to a service with that setting.

With no promise, the node can stop the instance with no wait. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=promise
name=stop-notice
notice=0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:f7bb973c68c1d1101fb628905ad68ed46453bf1c94c374628655cba7391bd3a3
rule=the node sends the notice at least value seconds before each stop or hibernation that the instance did not ask for
value=seconds, base 10
